From afa64844d403fef0e4963098d3d83ff98c441b84 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ake Rehnman <ake.rehnman@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 20:47:09 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] virtio-gpu: BUG FIX: separate global and context async fence
 completions

The async fence handler checks context and ring identity only for
commands carrying VIRTIO_GPU_FLAG_INFO_RING_IDX. A context fence callback
can therefore retire unrelated global commands with lower or equal
fence IDs, reporting completion prematurely.

Require global commands to be completed by the legacy callback,
identified by context 0 and ring UINT32_MAX. This preserves the timeline
separation already enforced by the synchronous fence callbacks.

*** This is a general QEMU correctness fix, not specific to Yttrium. ***
*** No observed Yttrium runtime failure has been traced to this bug. ***
---
 hw/display/virtio-gpu-virgl.c | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/hw/display/virtio-gpu-virgl.c b/hw/display/virtio-gpu-virgl.c
index 6e298f997d6..2aa1a728b85 100644
--- a/hw/display/virtio-gpu-virgl.c
+++ b/hw/display/virtio-gpu-virgl.c
@@ -1261,6 +1261,8 @@ static void virtio_gpu_virgl_async_fence_bh(void *opaque)
                 if (cmd->cmd_hdr.ctx_id != f->ctx_id) {
                     continue;
                 }
+            } else if (f->ctx_id != 0 || f->ring_idx != UINT32_MAX) {
+                continue;
             }
             virtio_gpu_ctrl_response_nodata(g, cmd, VIRTIO_GPU_RESP_OK_NODATA);
             QTAILQ_REMOVE(&g->fenceq, cmd, next);
